=== AUTHENTICATION (login + passwords) ===

THE IDEA (nightclub):
- signup   = get on the guest list (make an account)
- login    = show ID, get a wristband (token)
- protected route = bouncer checks your wristband before letting you in

PASSWORD HASHING (auth.py):
- NEVER store the real password - store scrambled gibberish
- hash_password("mypass123") -> "$2b$12$...gibberish..." (one-way, can't reverse)
- verify_password(typed, stored) -> True/False (does it match?)
- even if hacker steals the database, they see gibberish not passwords

JWT TOKEN (the wristband):
- login checks password -> if correct, hands out a token
- token has user_id hidden inside it
- jwt.encode(...) makes it, jwt.decode(...) reads it
- SECRET_KEY signs it so nobody can fake one

PROTECTED ROUTE:
- get_current_user = the bouncer (a HELPER function, no @app route)
- reads token from header -> decodes it -> finds the user
- used via Depends(get_current_user), same as Depends(get_db)
- no token = blocked (401). valid token = come in

HELPER vs ROUTE:
- answers a URL? -> needs @app. route
- helps other functions? -> no route, called via Depends
- get_db and get_current_user are both helpers

